  "final_message": "Refunding a paid invoice now returns the money instead of raising `InvalidStateError: invoice has no successful payment to refund`. The full suite passes (25 tests).\n\n**Root cause:** In `refund_invoice` (`billing/refunds.py`), the code called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function takes an invoice ID and looks up payments by `invoice_id`, so passing the customer ID matched nothing. The refund loop skipped every payment, `refunded` stayed at 0, and the function raised the misleading error even though the charge had succeeded.\n\n**Fix:** One line in `billing/refunds.py`: the call now passes `invoice_id`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_refund_paid_invoice_returns_money` to `tests/test_credit_notes.py`. It fails on the old code and passes with the fix.\n\n**Answer file:** `answer.json` in the repo root contains `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`. It doesn't appear in `git status`, so it's probably covered by `.gitignore`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
